Speaking as someone who has killed the Balrog, no wiz mode, with a female
elf ranger, I would like to say that even though none of my hack characters
have survided past level 10, I've had more fun than the two months or so of
playing Moria.

Quite simply, Moria is more hack and slash than Hack; beating the balrog
(since it was made tougher but not more interesting) isn't hard but it is
booring. You simply play for 30 hours or so on end being able to kill 
everything but the balrog below level 25 in order to get the kajillion or
so potions of invulnerability/scrolls of Rune of Protection and the 4d6
+10,+10 Zweihander you need to turn him into balrogburgers.

Hack: It's more fun. I've been killed more total in the past two weeks than
I ever had playing Moria, where you don't dare die (i.e. you cheat like hell
restoring save files) because it's taken you 40 hours of game time to get 
where you are...

In brief: You become demigod when you win Hack.
You become demigod in order to win Moria. And it feels like it takes years.

